The cell 'span occurring twice in the document / value differing from the span by case' specifies that the span appears at least twice in the document and the value differs from the span only in case. For the kernel `conformance.kernel.grounding`, the rule states it provides the grounding verdict with "no relaxation, value-in-span checked" [6ab8417a77f3b613]. Because 'no relaxation' is specified for the value-in-span check, a value that differs from the span by case is not considered to be in the span, implying a verdict of VALUE_NOT_IN_SPAN. In the rewritten text, I change the value to match the span character for character. The rule then implies a verdict of GROUNDED. Thus, the verdict moves.
